  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "BUILD inside the autopilot",
      "items": [
        "FL_Mission / ModeFeatherLane are candidate names, not existing or implemented upstream modules.",
        "Our C++ extension owns in-flight mission state, observation freshness, stop/continue policy and mission events.",
        "The mode adapter reuses navigation/controllers. Existing arming, manual override and failsafe semantics must be qualified and retained.",
        "Mission-selected capabilities: coordinate/route tasks need no target detector; object-dependent steps require qualified perception/localization."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "REUSE and explicit interfaces",
      "items": [
        "Stock AUTO / AP_Mission and GUIDED remain baseline choices. Only the selected mode runs; custom behavior does not imply simultaneous AUTO execution.",
        "The new mission/observation API and handler mapping remain unqualified; stock Guided messages do not automatically target the custom mode.",
        "External perception supplies timestamped goals/estimates. No blocking inference, browser work or slow I/O belongs in critical callbacks."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Maintenance and evidence",
      "items": [
        "Maintain identifiable custom commits against pinned upstream/submodules. Review integrations and requalify before adopting an update.",
        "Native placement removes a process/message boundary for internal decisions; end-to-end latency benefit remains unmeasured.",
        "Maintained core design. Native placement is user-confirmed; exact names, message contracts and timing budgets remain proposed. Current learning progress is recorded in the phase registry."
      ]
    }
  ]
